<section class="services">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Public record — retrievable</p>
    <h2>What's generally on the public docket</h2>
    <div class="svc-grid">
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>The Docket Sheet</h3><p>Every filing in the case, in order, with dates. The index everything else is organized against.</p></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>Indictment or Information</h3><p>The charging document — what the government alleged and under which statutes.</p></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>Judgment &amp; Commitment Order</h3><p>The court's final order: the sentence imposed, the conditions, and the statutory basis.</p></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>Plea Agreement</h3><p>If the case resolved by plea, the written agreement and the change-of-plea hearing transcript when ordered.</p></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>Sentencing Transcript</h3><p>The record of what was argued and said at sentencing — often the single most useful document for post-conviction work.</p></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="cite">Retrievable</span><h3>Notice of Appeal &amp; Appellate Record</h3><p>If the case was appealed: the notice, the parties' briefs, and the circuit's opinion or order, where one exists.</p></div>
